<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Centre Party (Finland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1906">1906</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Agrarian League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Centre Party is a Finnish political party founded in 1906 as the Agrarian League to represent small farmers and rural areas. It became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>'s three main parties and led many governments; its most prominent figure, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urho-kekkonen">Urho Kekkonen</a>, was prime minister several times and president from 1956 to 1982. It was renamed the Centre Party in 1965.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/centre-party-finland.jpg" alt="Centre Party (Finland)" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Centre Party of Finland · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keskusta_2026.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
